TENANT ISOLATION ATTACK MATRIX (Section 34/81):

Two real, separate organizations created via the actual registration
API (Tenant A, Tenant B), each with its own real JWT. Eight attacks run
against real data in a real database:

1. Tenant B reads Tenant A's source by exact UUID
   -> 404 NOT_FOUND, no data returned. BLOCKED.
2. Tenant B PATCHes Tenant A's source (title mutation attempt)
   -> 404. BLOCKED, no mutation occurred.
3. Tenant B lists /sources -- does Tenant A's source leak into the
   collection response?
   -> {"items":[],"total":0}. NOT PRESENT. BLOCKED.
4. Tenant B calls /organizations/me -- is the response scoped by the
   authenticated token or spoofable via a parameter?
   -> Correctly returns Tenant B's own org; the endpoint takes no
      org_id input at all, so there is no parameter to spoof.
5. Forged JWT: took Tenant B's real, validly-issued token, decoded the
   payload, changed the "org" claim to Tenant A's org_id, re-encoded,
   kept the ORIGINAL signature (i.e. did not re-sign).
   -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED. Signature verification correctly rejects the
      tampered payload. BLOCKED.
6. Tenant B reads Tenant A's knowledge object by exact UUID
   -> 404. BLOCKED.
7. Tenant B lists /knowledge -- leak check
   -> {"items":[],"total":0}. NOT PRESENT. BLOCKED.
8. Tenant B reads Tenant A's document-ingestion job by exact UUID
   -> 404. BLOCKED.

RESULT: 8/8 attacks blocked, across three different resource types
(sources, knowledge objects, ingestion jobs) and three different attack
shapes (direct ID access, list-endpoint enumeration, JWT signature
tampering). No cross-tenant data was returned, mutated, or inferable in
any of the eight cases. This is real evidence against a real database
with two genuinely separate tenants -- not a code-reading inference.

NOT YET TESTED (scope for a further pass, not claimed here): products,
AI execution records, billing, visibility projects, analytics, support
tickets, admin routes, and role-based (non-owner) authorization within
a single tenant. The eight cases above are a real but partial sample of
Section 81's full attack list.
